          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"bronte-jane-eyre-8d223e8c973ddc84\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":3,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.9,\"analysis\":\"The verbalised look primarily avows St. John’s love as an existing emotional state. It also has substantial expressive/reflexive force because his involuntary bodily response is presented as his repressed feeling manifesting itself despite his effort to remain silent. It does not undertake a relationship; the imagined continuation explicitly represents him as withholding an offer of his heart.\",\"ambiguity\":\"E is somewhat interpretively mediated: St. John produces no words, and Jane converts his involuntary expression into a detailed propositional speech. Nevertheless, the underlying communicative event is strongly framed as affect escaping repression.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"nonverbal_verbalised\",\"description\":\"Jane renders what St. John’s sad, resolute look seems to communicate; he does not say the quoted words with his lips.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Jane interprets St. John’s trembling hand, burning eye, and expressive look as a silent confession to Rosamond. His love is represented as genuine and mutually viable, but subordinated to his religious vocation: he believes Rosamond would accept him, yet refuses to offer himself because his heart is already metaphorically sacrificed to missionary duty.\" ,\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“He seemed to say, with his sad and resolute look, if he did not say it with his lips”\",\"supports\":\"Identifies the event as Jane’s verbalisation of nonverbal communication rather than an actual spoken declaration.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I love you, and I know you prefer me.”\",\"supports\":\"Strongly supports truth-conditional avowal of a loving emotional state.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“he could not, conceal it from her”; “his hand would tremble and his eye burn”\",\"supports\":\"Supports expressive/reflexive force: his affect manifests involuntarily despite attempted stoic restraint.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“If I offered my heart, I believe you would accept it. But that heart is already laid on a sacred altar”\",\"supports\":\"The offer is counterfactual and withheld, weighing strongly against performative commitment.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"St. John “would not” relinquish his missionary vocation for Rosamond’s love.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms that the silent avowal acknowledges feeling without undertaking a romantic union.\",\"confidence\":0.97}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T captures the avowed state, while E captures the involuntary manifestation of repressed affect. P is appropriately absent because the passage stresses St. John’s refusal to make a relational offer; no residual core force requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The quoted speech is Jane’s interpretive expansion of St. John’s look, not a verbatim utterance by him.\"}"
        }
      ],
